WEBVTT

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.090
This is a tale from long, long ago.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.320
Our Highland Kingdom 
was once the land of the fairies.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.770
The fairies loved peace.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.280
They loved beautiful things and fun things...

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:20.040
and so they lived quietly 
and peacefully for hundreds of years.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.360
But I feel so sorry for the poor fairies now.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.540
Yes, the poor fairies.

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.540
This is all because 500 years ago...

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:36.370
humans rose in rebellion 
and made the fairies their servants.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:44.300
People say that fairies were fools who 
idled away their time and lost to the humans,

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.100
but Mama doesn't think that's true.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.570
There are fewer fairies than humans,

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:54.490
so in a contest of strength, 
they lost to the humans. That's all.

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:57.530
Why do you think that, Mama?

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.990
Well, just look!

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.180
How beautiful!

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:13.910
Here.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:18.050
It's delicious!

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:20.840
Sugar confections are a sacred food.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.540
They extend the lifespans of fairies 
and bring good fortune to humans.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:29.340
And the first ones to make 
these sugar confections were fairies.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.060
Really?

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:34.200
And the method of refining 
sugar apples into silver sugar...

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.400
was discovered by fairies.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.700
That's how sugar confections were born.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.640
And that is why sugar artisans...

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:45.530
most especially silver sugar masters, 
must never look down on fairies.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.220
They must keep company 
with fairies as friends.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:49.920
And so must you, Anne.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:52.450
I will!

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.870
<i>Mama, watch over me!</i>

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.930
<i>I will become a silver sugar master 
just like you were!</i>

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.520
All right, I'm setting out!

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.920
Wait! Anne!

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:33.420
Huh?

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:35.130
What?

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:37.090
Wait for me, Anne!

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.090
J-Jonas?!

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:41.280
You're just awful, 
leaving without saying a word like that.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.360
I-I'm sorry. If I said goodbye, 
I thought you'd try to stop me.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.310
Even though you didn't say it, 
I still came to stop you.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:51.560
Jonas, I'm truly grateful to you 
for everything up until now.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.750
Your family and the people 
of this village were truly good to Mama.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.850
But I did tell you, didn't I?

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:59.960
I want to enter this year's 
Sugar Confectionary Exhibition.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.280
No. I must enter, no matter what.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.410
Please understand!

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.760
I <i>do</i> understand!

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.780
I'm a sugar artisan too!

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.960
But it will be impossible for you 
to travel all the way to Lewiston alone.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.850
After all, you're small for being fifteen.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.400
You're as scrawny as a scarecrow,

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.130
and your entire fortune consists of 
that run-down cart and the horse.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.030
But I love you just as you are.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:22.090
So, won't you marry me?

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.340
I told you! Ever since the day 
you and your mother first came here,

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.330
I have been completely entranced by you.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:31.600
I will fill the hole that 
has been left in your heart!

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.500
I will make you as happy 
as your mother did and more!

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.850
After all, I come from a wealthy house.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:39.890
And we're related by blood to the founder 
of the Radcliffe Workshop school...

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.490
Anne! Wait!

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.700
Goodbye, Jonas! Take care!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.660
Anne! Wait! Anne!

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.260
<i>Jonas would never seriously propose to me.</i>

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:56.630
<i>He pities me because 
I've lost Mama, that's all.</i>

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.900
<i>To marry out of pity would be so...</i>

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.200
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.970
<i>The thought of marriage itself, 
of living as someone's wife...</i>

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.520
<i>I want to live my own life!</i>

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.430
<i>I want to chase my dreams!</i>

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:15.700
<i>Right, Mama?</i>

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:22.010
Take that, you piece of crap.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.730
Excuse me, what's going...

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:25.500
You little...

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:29.540
Take that, you malicious little...

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.410
A fairy?!

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:35.170
A labor fairy who serves 
that fairy hunter there.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:38.430
He stole his own wing and tried to escape.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.590
You thief of a fairy.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.670
This is what I'll do 
to the likes of your wing.

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:45.380
D-Don't!

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.610
How horrible!

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:54.370
A fairy's wing is its life!

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.100
Why won't anyone save him?

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.270
Well, because he's a fairy.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.680
And the fairy hunter 
has a violent personality.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:04.250
If your attempt to help went badly, 
and then he turned on you...

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.080
How's that?

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.490
Never defy me again, understand?

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.200
Swear that you'll never steal 
your wing and try to run away again.

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:08.200
H-Hey...

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.960
Hmph! Who'd swear anything to a human?

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:15.090
I'll take it back again 
and again! It's my wing!

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:18.730
Very well! 
Then, I'll just kill you right here.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.420
If you'll excuse me?

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:20.630
Ready and...

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:21.550
there!

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:30.630
Here you are.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:36.310
Oh, wait!

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:39.820
Bah! I'd never thank the likes of a human!

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.270
And don't you forget it!

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:48.340
Well... yes. I am one of those 
detestable humans, after all, right?

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:52.260
You! You let my valuable labor fairy escape!

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:53.680
What are you gonna do about it?

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:57.180
Well, you were planning 
to kill that fairy, weren't you?

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:59.830
That's no different from
 him leaving like this.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:02.000
Little girl, you...

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.800
Hey! That's enough!

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:07.010
A grown man like you raising 
your hand against a child like her?

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:10.490
It may have only been a fairy, 
but you were a little too awful to it!

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:11.690
That's right!

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:12.640
I won't forget this.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:13.890
Go on! Get out of here!

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.180
Serves you right!

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.160
You're very impressive, young lady.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:16.910
And don't come back!

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.280
To put that tiny body of yours 
on the line for a fairy...

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:20.730
It was my pleasure.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:24.250
Despite how I look, I'm fifteen. 
In this kingdom, that's the age of majority.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.570
I beg your pardon.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:28.360
Still, you're a very kind girl.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:33.620
About that... The truth is that I'm not.

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:39.060
Sir, where can I find the fairy market?

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:46.290
Labor fairies! They're hard workers!

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:49.010
Would you like a companion fairy? 
I have a collection of beauties!

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:52.090
Come, come! Keep hold of one of their wings 
and fairies will do whatever you want!

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.260
Come and buy!

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:55.600
Would you happen to have 
any warrior fairies for sale?

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.930
I don't carry anything as dangerous as that.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.340
The old man down at the end does have one.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:03.880
But you should give up on it. 
It's defective goods.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:04.900
Thank you.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:43.140
<i>Beautiful...</i>

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:45.310
<i>just doesn't do justice to him.</i>

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:48.340
<i>I've never seen a fairy like him.</i>

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:51.250
I thought I saw something familiar...

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:52.340
but it's just a scarecrow.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.390
A scarecrow?

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:56.590
You. I'm talking about you.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.250
That's right, Scarecrow.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:02.890
S-S-Scarecrow?!

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:05.580
That is so rude!
You can't say that to a girl in her prime!

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:08.050
Who cares anything 
for the prime of a scarecrow?

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.340
H-How dare you speak that way...

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.080
Sorry about that, young miss.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.540
My goods have a sharp tongue.

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:20.270
If anyone passes by, he calls them names 
with no care for who they are.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:21.700
Pay it no mind 
and continue on your way.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:22.770
But I do mind!

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:25.060
This advice may be unwelcome,

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:28.290
but with a tongue like that, 
you'll never sell him as a companion fairy!

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:30.170
Why don't you just let him go?

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.460
That's not a companion fairy.

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:34.970
It's a warrior fairy.

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:35.570
What?

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:41.380
Three fairy hunters died capturing him. 
That's what an excellent article he is.

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.970
Th-That can't be true!

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:47.040
The warrior fairies I've seen up until now 
have been burlier and bigger...

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:50.160
For a fairy trader, 
trust is the most important thing.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.760
We don't lie.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:55.700
Um, I came to buy a warrior fairy, but...

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.560
Don't you have anyone besides him?

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:00.400
Warrior fairies are difficult to handle.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:04.440
This one is the only one I have for sale. 
You could try somewhere else.

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.250
Hey, Scarecrow.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:09.410
By "scarecrow," do you mean me?

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:11.130
Is there anyone here but you?

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:13.500
Stop dithering.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:14.440
Buy me.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:17.410
B-Buy... Are you giving me an order?

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:19.640
Marvelous!

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:23.340
This is the first time I've heard him 
tell someone to buy him.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:26.330
Could it be that you fell in love 
with the young miss at first sight?

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:26.910
What?

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.340
Don't assume that I am like you.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:30.380
What?

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:34.340
I said not to assume that 
I am like you, you filthy human.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:37.590
Don't!

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.440
Wait! What are you doing? Stop!

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:47.470
Please. Please!

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:48.160
One hundred cress!

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:48.870
What?

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.320
I believe this should satisfy you.

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:04.870
A gold coin?

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.750
That's quite a show of commitment 
from you, young miss.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.720
But you've made a good purchase here.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:11.020
Here. His wing. 
Go on and verify the goods yourself.

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:25.550
This is...

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:33.060
My heart.

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:36.980
Now, be very careful, understand?

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:39.000
Warrior fairies are savage.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:41.960
Let down your guard, and he'll immediately 
steal that leather pouch...

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:43.830
and come to kill you.

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:45.400
That isn't all.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:48.300
I'll come to kill you, too. Just wait.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:48.980
Hey!

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:51.180
I look forward to it.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:55.480
Excuse me! I wish you'd stop speaking 
as though it's certain that I'll be killed!

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:56.940
Come on. We're going!

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:05.210
Say, young miss! Are you really going to 
be able to make him serve you?

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:07.440
Of course she can. Right, Scarecrow?

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.100
It's Anne! Anne Halford!

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:12.230
The next time you call me that,
 I'll hit you, understand?

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:19.690
I'm headed to Lewiston from here.

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:21.950
I'd like for you to protect me 
on my way there.

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:25.160
In other words, provide escort. 
May I ask that of you?

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:29.280
A simple task. I'll even throw in 
a kiss as a special service.

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:32.050
I do not require 
any such high-handed service!

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:34.140
Least of all my precious...

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:36.860
You haven't had your first kiss yet, either? 
You're such a child.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:40.270
Well, pardon me for being a child! 
And anyway, you...

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:44.640
What is your name?

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:46.340
Why do you want to know?

00:11:46.340 --> 00:11:49.850
Well, I don't know 
what I should call you, do I?

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:54.540
Tom or Sam. Call me by 
whatever human name you like.

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.570
Then I'll call you Crow.

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:58.460
In retaliation for calling you Scarecrow?

00:11:58.460 --> 00:12:00.170
That's right, Mister Crow.

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:04.860
Shall Fen Shall.

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:09.560
Shall Fen Shall. That's a beautiful name.

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:11.890
Which part is your first name 
and which is your surname?

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:13.450
The entirety is my name.

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:15.920
We do not differentiate between 
first and last names like humans do.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:19.410
Really? But Shall Fen Shall 
is too long, so...

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:21.970
I'll call you Shall. Is that all right?

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.600
I believe I told you to call me 
whatever you like.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.430
You are my master.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:29.340
Yes, I am.

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:34.080
<i>Wings are the source 
of a fairy's life force.</i>

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:36.150
<i>Even if their wings are 
ripped off, they can survive.</i>

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:39.100
<i>But if their wings are damaged, 
they weaken and die.</i>

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:44.140
<i>Having learned that, humans rip off 
a single wing to force fairies to obey them.</i>

00:12:44.140 --> 00:12:45.950
<i>That is how fairies ended up serving humans.</i>

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:51.180
I bought you because I wanted you 
to serve as my guard, Shall.

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:52.930
But I promise you this...

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:55.950
once we arrive in Lewiston, 
I will return your wing to you.

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:58.520
You're saying you will set me free?

00:12:58.520 --> 00:12:59.290
That's right.

00:12:59.780 --> 00:13:02.400
You'll allow a fairy which you bought 
with a gold coin to escape?

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:04.510
Could such a naïve human exist?

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:06.260
Naïve?

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:10.730
I simply believe that humans 
and fairies can be friends, that's all.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.610
The truth is, I don't want to 
compel anyone to serve me.

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:16.140
And, of course, I don't want to 
sell you to another human.

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:18.230
That's why I'll return your wing to you.

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:21.550
And while you're accompanying me 
on my travels like this,

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:24.670
I'd like to treat you 
as a friend, if that's possible.

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:26.450
Friends?

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:28.660
We could never become friends.

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:33.590
My mama and me, it's our ideal...

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:36.350
for humans and fairies 
to treat each other as equals.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:38.680
But if no one ever 
actually puts it into practice,

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:41.190
then that ideal will never become reality.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.380
That's why I will do it.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:46.260
So both mother and daughter 
have the brains of scarecrows?

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:48.840
Please don't insult my mother!

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:59.900
If you hate me so much, 
why did you tell me to buy you?

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:03.690
I would never want to be made 
to serve someone I hated!

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:06.940
Humans are all the same.

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:10.420
In which case, being made to serve 
a fool makes things easier for me.

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:16.040
Amongst those I have seen in the last few 
years, you seemed the greatest fool by far.

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:13.300
The Bloody Highway.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:15.490
It's approximately 1,200 carron long.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:18.730
Between here and Lewiston, 
there isn't a single village or town.

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:22.090
There are merely fortshelters,
 a sort of convenient stronghold.

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:24.870
You'll also find wild animals
 that attack indiscriminately...

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.320
And bandits, of course.

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:27.730
You know this road?

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:31.210
How many years do you think 
I have been forced to serve humans?

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:35.060
And the reason you bought me was to 
help you make it through this road, wasn't it?

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:37.540
I'm depending on you, Mister Warrior Fairy.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.280
You should pray as hard as you can...

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:44.700
that we reach the first fortshelter safely.

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:49.950
Here, it's for you.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:55.250
I know.

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:59.310
Our luck just happened to be good today.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:03.630
But this journey is a long one. 
If the worst happens, I'll be counting on you.

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:14.990
<i>He is vexing, but...</i>

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:18.250
fairy wings are beautiful, aren't they?

00:16:19.690 --> 00:16:20.980
May I touch it?

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:24.520
Don't touch me!

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:27.170
Everything other than what 
you hold in your hands is mine.

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:28.530
I'm sorry.

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:30.910
That was thoughtless of me.

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:34.110
<i>Why did I do that?</i>

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:36.630
<i>I thought I understood, but...</i>

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:47.150
Mama!

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:50.190
Anne! Awake already?

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:56.410
Oh my. What's wrong?

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:57.850
Are you hurt somewhere?

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:00.370
It's not that. I had a horrible dream.

00:17:00.820 --> 00:17:03.510
Mama, you had died. It was a horrible dream.

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:05.220
You silly.

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:11.180
Find your life's path and walk it resolutely.

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:13.740
Mama?

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:15.180
I know you can do it.

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:18.060
You're such a good girl, Anne. Don't cry.

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:19.680
Wait... Wait, Mama!

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:22.680
Please, Mama! Don't go!

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:30.970
Wh-What...

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:34.190
What, what, what, what, what?

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:36.750
What do you want? 
Just now, your hand was on my neck.

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:40.270
Shall, your wing. You couldn't have been...

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:41.740
I almost had it.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:42.940
You're heartless!

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:47.090
I told you didn't I? 
I want to be your friend!

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:48.380
And in spite of that, you...

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:52.290
Friends?

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:54.500
When you hold my life in your hands?

00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:58.890
I have been bought by you, 
forced to serve you.

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.050
We can never be friends.

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:04.550
I am a fool, aren't I?

00:18:07.550 --> 00:18:10.180
You're right. I've been naïve.

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:12.590
Even though I'd made up my mind 
to have you serve me,

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:15.530
I've kept saying selfish things 
about wanting to be friends.

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:18.150
I won't <i>ever</i> let down my guard again!

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:24.440
A bagworm moth this time, then, is it?

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:26.220
Scarecrow suits me just fine!

00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:27.410
And I'll say this as well.

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:29.560
Despite everything, I will keep my promise.

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:31.560
When we reach Lewiston, 
I'll return your wing.

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:34.980
Once I do, I'll ask you again 
whether or not we can be friends!

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:37.330
Until then, I am your master!

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:40.920
<i>I bungled that.</i>

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:43.250
<i>But there is no need to be impatient.</i>

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.500
<i>I've spent nearly 70 years 
being forced to serve humans.</i>

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:50.990
<i>My freedom may have been put off 
for a day, but three days from now...</i>

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:53.430
<i>There it is again.</i>

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:57.400
<i>Why does that scent come from this girl?</i>

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:00.850
<i>The sweet scent of silver sugar...</i>

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:03.980
<i>Liz...</i>

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:10.130
We must reach the next 
fortshelter within the day.

00:19:10.470 --> 00:19:13.030
We've traveled 200 carron 
since starting out on the highway.

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:15.550
That's still only a sixth of the distance.

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:18.210
Stop.

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:19.100
What?

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:25.970
Bandits?

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:28.770
Let's go!

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:31.250
Oh no! They're coming this way!

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:33.930
That's right! 
Shall, you're a warrior fairy, aren't you?

00:19:33.930 --> 00:19:35.700
Chase the bandits away!

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:36.690
That's too much work.

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:39.440
Too much work? Honestly! 
I'm your master! Your master!

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:41.650
At this rate, we'll be killed! Please!

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:44.370
What? You're too close!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:48.280
If you're my master, then you shouldn't plead. 
You should order me, shouldn't you?

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:51.160
You're too close! Please, move away! 
Just go, won't you?

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.060
Your face is red.

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:54.420
J-J-Just go, won't you? 
Please, I'm begging you!

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:56.760
I told you to give me an order.

00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:58.900
An order? But look, they're coming!

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:02.420
"Go, now." "I'll tear up your wing." 
If you said those things, I'd go immediately.

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:04.840
What are you talking about? Just, please!

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:08.770
Order me.

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:11.450
I said go! If you don't go, I'll punch you!

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:14.370
I suppose that will do. I'll go.

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:16.580
At your command, Mistress Scarecrow.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:23.700
Shall!

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:40.290
I-It's a warrior fairy! Turn back!

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:04.950
The Scarecrow and the Fairy

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:40.000
<b>The Bloody Highway</b>
